course: dictionary
lesson: 11164
title: The windowsill
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A windowsill is the flat shelf at the bottom of a window. It can be inside the room or outside the glass. People put plants, ornaments and cups on it.
explain: Windowsills are great places for science. «Put a broad bean in a jam jar with wet paper towel on the windowsill» and you can watch it swell, split and grow a root and a shoot.
explain: A windowsill is not a place to climb or sit. Never sit on the windowsill of an open upstairs window, because you could fall out.
fact: A windowsill is the flat shelf at the bottom of a window.
fact: «On the windowsill» means resting on that shelf, inside or outside the glass.
fact: «A sunny windowsill» is a good place to grow seeds and plants, because they need light.
fact: Plants on a windowsill bend towards the light, as «a cress plant on the windowsill leans towards the light».
fact: Never climb or sit on the windowsill of an open upstairs window: it is dangerous.
exercise: «Put a broad bean in a jam jar on the windowsill.» What is a windowsill? | A small seat inside a cupboard | A door that opens onto the garden | *A flat shelf at the bottom of a window | The glass part you can see through
exercise: Why should you never sit on the windowsill of an open upstairs window? | Because the windowsill is for cups only | *Because you could fall out and get badly hurt | Because it keeps the room warm | Because the glass is too thin to see through
exercise: «Put a pondweed leaf in a glass of water on a sunny windowsill and watch: tiny bubbles rise from it.» What do the bubbles show? | The water is boiling | The leaf is sinking to the bottom | *The leaf is making oxygen in the sunlight | The leaf is dead
test: Which windowsill is best for growing seeds? | A dark cupboard | Inside a shoe box | *A sunny windowsill | Under the bed
test: «A cress plant on the windowsill leans towards the light.» What does the cress plant do? | Runs away from the sun | Turns into a stone | *Leans towards the light | Sinks into the soil
exam: «A dead bee on the windowsill will never move again, however gently Jayden pokes it.» What does this show? | A bee wakes up if you poke it gently | A windowsill makes bees come alive | Dead means it is only sleeping | *Dead means it will never move again, unlike a sleeping cat
